I agree with the advice that you've received so far, and it sounds
like things are going well.  The only advice that I would add is
related to reflection, rings and gold.

> 2. ring of slow digestion so I don't starve. (since I can ID this from
> sinks, will probably wait until
> actually starving)

By the mid-game, you'll have a good supply of rings and certainly by
the end you'll be tripping over them.  With the Eye you'll probably be
able to polymorph your supply into whatever collection you want if you
haven't found the rings by then anyway.  The only time I would
consider wishing for a ring is to achieve a conduct (e.g. ring of slow
digestion for food conduct), to get out of an annoying/hazardous
situation (e.g. ring of teleport control after tengu corpses left me
merely "jumpy"), to finish a game (e.g. wish for a ring of free action
to finish my Ascension Kit), or to make the game easier (e.g. ring of
slow digestion so that I don't have to pay as much attention to
nutrition).  There are other cases, I'm sure, but there are typically
more efficient ways to contribute towards survival than wishing for
rings.

If you're worried about food, in addition to the plethora of corpses
in your wake, you'll find at least two stashes: Sokoban and the
Castle.  Ludios, if it exists in your game, also has a lot.  Keep
those locations in mind as you cast your spells and go through
nutrition.  If you stay mindful you should be fine.

